jobs.description:
Are you looking for a fulltime job in logistics? Would you like to work in a modern, international warehouse where fashion and clothing products are shipped to customers all over the world? Then this opportunity could be perfect for you!

For a large logistics clothing warehouse in Lelystad, we are looking for motivated Production Workers, Warehouse Operatives, and Logistics Associates. You will become part of a friendly international team where teamwork, quality, and a positive working atmosphere are key. On top of that, you can enjoy a delicious hot lunch every working day.

As a Production Worker in the warehouse, you will help ensure that all goods are processed efficiently and accurately. Your tasks will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking and packing customer orders;
- Checking products for quality;
- Unpacking boxes and processing incoming goods;
- Sorting clothing and accessories;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

This is a full-time position in a 2-shift rotation:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM - 03:30 PM
- Afternoon shift: 03:00 PM - 11:30 PM

But there is also a nightshift you can work if you want from 23:00 tot 07:30. And there is work in the weekends!

- (Basic) English communication skills, or Polish or Spanish;
- Availability for full-time work in a 2-shift schedule;
- Ability to work effectively in a team;
- Physically fit and comfortable performing active warehouse work;
- Attention to detail and ability to follow instructions;
- Previous logistics or warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

Work in a international production team and help make high-quality products. You'll operate machines, check quality, and keep everything running smoothly. As a Production Employee, your tasks are broad and varied. While some tasks are repetitive, employees rotate weekly between different workstations and responsibilities. This ensures that you remain widely deployable, engaged, and continuously developing new skills.

What you'll do:

- Operating and monitoring production machines;
- Performing quality checks and completing required documentation;
- Counting, stamping, and registering production time;
- Preparing finished products and orders for shipping;
- Keeping your workspace clean, organized, and safe;
- Reporting deviations, malfunctions, or quality issues to your team leader.

You will work in three shifts:

- 06:00 – 14:00
- 14:00 – 22:00
- 22:00 – 06:00

- Good knowledge of the English language;
- Ability to work accurately and precisely – this is the most important requirement;
- Basic computer skills (data entry, forms, registrations);
- A focused mindset with the ability to work quickly and efficiently;
- Flexibility and willingness to learn and rotate between workstations;
- Availability and motivation to work in a 3- as well as a 2-shift system;
